Z||000003||Formula||06-07-2000||09:23 PM||||$289?????????? WTF<P>My whole system didnt cost that much and it probably hits really close to the same decibel rating.<BR>AND you can leave the car basically stock WITHOUT cutting holes in it.<P>heres what I recommend, Sony Xplod 10" $90, a Jensen 300w amp bridged to 400w peak load $100, and build a box like mine for under $20.<P>thats $210 for everything and its almost no labor.  The amp sits behind the passenger seat and the wires are incredibly easy to run.<P>If you port it into the cab you'll get a little bit more sound but my setup sounds perfectly good inside the car and you dont get any distortion inside the car.  <P>If you want anymore info then I can send it to you.  I'll get the dimensions tommorow.<P>btw...  there is almost a port into the cab with the windshield being so close to the sub, It does somehow (beyond me) travel fairly well into the cab even though there is a firewall there.<P>This has all been in my own opinion and what ever you do is up to you. but again, in my own opinion I think that subbox.com is a little bit of a steep price for minimal improvement. <p>[This message has been edited by Formula (edited 06-07-2000).]||||reg||1
